where winword also returned “Could not find files”, so Office isn't exposing WINWORD.EXE through PATH. That's normal and doesn't mean Office isn't installed.

Let's use the Office Click-to-Run registry instead. Run this in Administrator CMD:

reg query "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Office\ClickToRun\Configuration" /v ProductReleaseIds

Then:

reg query "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Office\ClickToRun\Configuration" /v InstallationPath

And:

reg query "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Office\ClickToRun\Configuration" /v ClientVersionToReport

Send me the output. From those three values I can identify exactly what Office 2021 edition is installed and where it is installed, then we'll check its activation channel.